 on the island of Savai'i in Samoa. It is situated on the east coast of the island in the district of Fa'asaleleaga and the electoral district of Fa'asaleleaga 3. The population is 205.","wpu":"Fatausi","img":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/a/a5/Fatausi-Village.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled"},{"n":"Lepea","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":-13.833333,"lo":-171.783333,"d":2353,"ds":"Lepea is a village on the island of Upolu in Samoa. The picturesque settlement of round Samoan houses built in a concentric pattern in large open grounds (malae) is situated 5 minutes drive west of the capital Apia on the north central coast of the island. It is part of the Tuamasaga electoral district.","wpu":"Lepea","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9a/Mt_Vaea_from_Lepea_village%2C_Samoa.JPG/960px-Mt_Vaea_from_Lepea_village%2C_Samoa.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Mulinuʻu","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":-13.816667,"lo":-171.783333,"d":2680,"ds":"Mulinuʻu is a small village situated on a tiny peninsula of Upolu island in Samoa. It became the site of the colonial administration in Samoa in the 1870s and continues to be the seat of government as the location of the Parliament of Samoa. It is located on the central-north coast of Upolu and is administratively part of the district of Tuamasaga and the urban area comprising Apia, the country's capital.","wpu":"Mulinuʻu","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f1/Mulinu%27u_by_Tattersall_Studios_-_Samoa_1893-1949.jpg/960px-Mulinu%27u_by_Tattersall_Studios_-_Samoa_1893-1949.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Vailima, Samoa","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":-13.865278,"lo":-171.761667,"d":4034,"ds":"Vailima is the name of a village on the island of Upolu, about four miles south of Apia, the capital of Samoa, the island nation in the Pacific Ocean. The population is 769. Vailima is part of the electoral political district of Tuamasaga.","wpu":"Vailima, Samoa","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/71/Robert_Lewis_Stevenson_Museum.jpg/960px-Robert_Lewis_Stevenson_Museum.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Mount Vaea","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":-13.863611,"lo":-171.773611,"d":4047,"ds":"Mount Vaea is a 472 m summit overlooking Apia, the capital of Samoa located on the north central coast of Upolu island. The mountain is situated south about 3 km inland from Apia township and harbour. The settlement at the foothills on the northern side of the mountain is called Lalovaea (below Vaea in Samoan).","wpu":"Mount Vaea","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/89/Round_Samoan_houses_with_blue_roofs%2C_Lepea_village_with_Mt_Vaea_beyond.JPG/960px-Round_Samoan_houses_with_blue_roofs%2C_Lepea_village_with_Mt_Vaea_beyond.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Baháʼí House of Worship of Samoa","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":-13.896706,"lo":-171.778312,"d":7731,"ds":"The Baháʼí House of Worship of Samoa is a Baháʼí House of Worship located in Tiapapata, inland from Apia, Samoa. The seventh Baháʼí House of Worship overall, it is the only Baháʼí temple in the Pacific islands, and thus is known by Baháʼís as the \"mother temple of the Pacific Islands.\" Construction of the temple began in 1981 and finished in 1984.","wpu":"Baháʼí House of Worship of Samoa","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/59/To_the_Temple_of_Gods_%2830379139910%29.jpg/960px-To_the_Temple_of_Gods_%2830379139910%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Upolu","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":-13.916667,"lo":-171.75,"d":9833,"ds":"Upolu is an island in Samoa, formed by a massive basaltic shield volcano which rises from the seafloor of the western Pacific Ocean. The island is 75 kilometres (47 miles) long and 1,125 square kilometres (434 square miles) in area, making it the second largest of the Samoan Islands by area. With approximately 145,000 inhabitants, it is by far the most populous of the Samoan Islands.","wpu":"Upolu","img":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/c/ce/Samoa_Country_map.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled"}],"about":{"ds":"Apia (Samoan: [a.pi.a]) is the capital and largest city of Samoa. It is located on the central north coast of Upolu, Samoa's second-largest island. Apia falls within the political district (itūmālō) of Tuamasaga.","wpu":"Apia","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/a/a8/WS-apia-regierg.jpg/960px-WS-apia-regierg.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},"wk":"2026-10-18"}